## 5. Capabilities at a Glance

| Capability | Potential value | Important limitation |
|---|---|---|
| Drive identification | Establishes device identity and reported firmware information | May be incomplete or inconsistent in a fault state |
| Status and log reading | Provides diagnostic evidence | Requires model-aware interpretation |
| SMART inspection | Offers selected health indicators | Does not rule out every type of failure |
| Service-area inspection | Helps examine supported internal structures | Availability and meaning vary by drive family |
| Firmware-module reading | Allows inspection of selected firmware-related data | Reading does not prove corruption or justify rewriting |
| Vendor-specific commands | Provides additional diagnostic or service functions | Some commands change state or have strict preconditions |
| Supported service procedures | May address a defined fault under suitable conditions | Not universal and not automatically safe |
| Imaging support | Helps preserve readable sectors | Cannot guarantee recovery of physically unreadable data |
| File-system analysis | Helps reconstruct logical access to files | Often requires separate tools and an image or clone |

This table describes general capability categories, not a feature guarantee for any particular product.

Always consult current documentation for the exact tool version, drive family, and operation under consideration.

