## Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **Adaptive data** | Drive-specific parameters used by some designs to account for characteristics of the individual mechanism or heads. |
| **Firmware module** | A logical unit of firmware-related code or data, where the platform uses such a structure. |
| **Imaging** | Creating a sector-level copy of a storage device or selected readable regions. |
| **ROM** | Read-only memory or a related non-volatile region containing code or device-specific information, depending on the design. |
| **Service area** | Reserved storage used by the drive for internal firmware-related structures or metadata, depending on the architecture. |
| **Translator** | A mechanism or data structure involved in mapping logical block addresses to the drive's physical storage layout. |
| **User data** | The sectors and file contents the owner is trying to retrieve. |

## Further Reading

For any specific drive or tool, prioritize current manufacturer documentation and the tool vendor's own compatibility notes. Community case reports can provide useful practical context, but a procedure that worked on one model or firmware revision should not be assumed safe for another.

When comparing claims, look for the exact model, firmware generation, symptoms, operation performed, and verified data outcome. These details matter more than a generic claim that a tool supports a particular manufacturer.

